<!--
  Snippet for the Wazuh AGENT's /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf, for when
  yubihsm-auditor runs on the same host as the agent (the common case: no
  syslog listener to open on the manager, no network hop, no TLS to set up —
  the agent ships the events over its existing encrypted channel).

  Pairs with yubihsm-auditor's `file` output:
    [output]
    type = "file"
    path = "/var/log/yubihsm/audit.jsonl"
    rotate_bytes = 134217728
    rotate_keep = 5

  Merge the <localfile> block into the agent's existing <ossec_config>, then
  restart the agent (systemctl restart wazuh-agent). Wazuh's JSON log format
  parses each line natively - no custom decoder needed, unlike the syslog
  path (decoders/local_decoder.xml). Rule field matching uses the bare key
  names (e.g. <field name="event_type">), same as the syslog path - see
  rules/local_rules-agent.xml. (archives.json/alerts.json nest the decoded
  fields under a `data` object for display, but that's just output
  serialization; <field name="..."> in a rule addresses them by their bare
  name regardless - confirmed with `wazuh-logtest`, whose Phase 2 output
  prints bare names like `collector: '...'`.) Install one rule set or the
  other, not both, per event stream - rules/local_rules-agent.xml for this
  path, rules/local_rules.xml for the syslog-to-manager path.

  Wazuh only tails the active file, so rotated files
  (audit.jsonl.1, .2, ...) are never re-read - matching yubihsm-auditor's own
  delivery guarantee that nothing is lost on a restart (see the project
  README's "Delivery guarantees" section).
-->
<ossec_config>
  <localfile>
    <log_format>json</log_format>
    <location>/var/log/yubihsm/audit.jsonl</location>
  </localfile>
</ossec_config>
